      "stem": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "If w + 1 = 4, what is the value of w?"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "1"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "3"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "5"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "B"
      },
      "solution": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1. isolate variable: Recognize that 1 is being added to w on the left side; to isolate w, apply the inverse operation (subtraction) to both sides."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2. subtract constant: Subtract 1 from both sides: w + 1 − 1 = 4 − 1."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "3. simplify: The left side reduces to w and the right side reduces to 3, giving w = 3."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        }
      ],
