      "type": "mcq",
      "stem": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "A geologist studying rock formations measures the thickness of two sediment layers in a drill core. The lower layer has a thickness of 16/2 centimeters, and the upper layer has an unknown thickness of n centimeters. If the total combined thickness of the two layers is 20 centimeters, what is the value of n?"
        }
      ],
      "options": [
        {
          "key": "A",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "4"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "B",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "12"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "C",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "18"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "28"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "B"
      },
      "solution": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1. isolate variable: Translate the geological context into an equation: the upper-layer thickness n plus the lower-layer thickness 16/2 equals the total thickness 20, giving n + 16/2 = 20."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2. simplify: Simplify the fraction appearing in the equation: 16/2 = 8, so the equation becomes n + 8 = 20. No fraction arithmetic carries forward."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "3. subtract constant: Subtract 8 from both sides of n + 8 = 20: n = 20 − 8 = 12."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "4. divide coefficient: The coefficient of n is 1; dividing both sides by 1 is trivial and confirms n = 12."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        }
      ],
