            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "key": "D",
          "seg": [
            {
              "t": "text",
              "v": "40"
            }
          ]
        }
      ],
      "answer": {
        "correct": "B"
      },
      "solution": [
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "1. isolate variable: Translate the word problem into an equation. Nine batches of h gallons on the left; 40 gallons more than one batch on the right: 9h = h + 40."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "2. move variable term: Subtract h from both sides to consolidate variable terms: 9h − h = h + 40 − h, giving 8h = 40."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        },
        {
          "t": "text",
          "v": "3. divide coefficient: Divide both sides by the coefficient 8: h = 40 ÷ 8 = 5."
        },
        {
          "t": "br"
        }
      ],
